---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Methodology — PickNotch" description="How PickNotch reviews and scores products. Our scoring system, what we look at, and how affiliate links work.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h1>How PickNotch reviews products</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">Our process, our scoring system, and why we always look for the catch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="method-body wrap-narrow">

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>What we look at</h2>
      <p>PickNotch doesn't rank products by spec sheet. We evaluate products across six categories:</p>
      <div class="criteria-grid">
        {[
          { n: '01', title: 'Value for money',       body: 'Does the price reflect the actual product quality, usability, and long-term cost? A cheap product can score highly here if the trade-offs are clear.' },
          { n: '02', title: 'Build & spec quality',  body: 'Materials, components, engineering decisions. Does the product do what its specs suggest? Are the specs honest?' },
          { n: '03', title: 'Real-world usability',  body: 'How does it actually perform? Not in ideal conditions — in normal, mixed real-world use. Range, speed, comfort, reliability.' },
          { n: '04', title: 'Brand & support',       body: 'Will the brand be there in 12 months? Is there a service network? How are warranty claims handled? This matters more than most buyers realise.' },
          { n: '05', title: 'Comfort & design',      body: 'Ergonomics, weight, aesthetics, and how the product fits into its intended use context.' },
          { n: '06', title: 'Downsides & risk',      body: 'Every product has a catch. We find it and score it separately. A high score here means real risk. A low score means minor issues.' },
        ].map(({ n, title, body }) => (
          <div class="criteria-card">
            <span class="criteria-n">{n}</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="criteria-title">{title}</h3>
              <p class="criteria-body">{body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>How scoring works</h2>
      <p>The PickNotch Score is a weighted composite of the six criteria above. Scores run from 0–10:</p>
      <div class="score-guide">
        {[
          { range: '9.0 – 10', label: 'Outstanding', desc: 'Best in class. Worth buying with confidence.' },
          { range: '8.0 – 8.9', label: 'Very good', desc: 'Strong all-rounder. Minor trade-offs only.' },
          { range: '7.0 – 7.9', label: 'Good',      desc: 'Solid choice for the right buyer. Some real trade-offs.' },
          { range: '5.5 – 6.9', label: 'Average',   desc: 'Acceptable but not recommended. Notable weaknesses.' },
          { range: '< 5.5',    label: 'Poor',       desc: 'Avoid. Significant issues outweigh the positives.' },
        ].map(({ range, label, desc }) => (
          <div class="sg-row">
            <span class="sg-range">{range}</span>
            <span class="sg-label">{label}</span>
            <span class="sg-desc">{desc}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="method-note">Scores are not rounded to make products look better. An 8.6 is an 8.6, not "almost a 9".</p>
    </section>

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>Why we include "The catch"</h2>
      <p>Every review on PickNotch includes a dedicated "The catch" section. This is mandatory, not optional. It explains:</p>
      <ul class="method-list">
        <li>The most significant weakness or risk in the product</li>
        <li>Who that weakness will matter most to</li>
        <li>Whether that weakness is a dealbreaker, a nuisance, or just a known trade-off</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We believe every honest review should tell you why <em>not</em> to buy, not just why to buy.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>Researched reviews vs hands-on reviews</h2>
      <p>We are transparent about the basis of each review:</p>
      <div class="review-type-grid">
        <div class="rt-card rt-card--published">
          <h3>Published review</h3>
          <p>A full review with a PickNotch Score. Based on thorough research: spec analysis, owner feedback, brand research, price benchmarking, and editorial judgement.</p>
          <p class="rt-note"><strong>Important:</strong> We do not claim hands-on testing unless we actually tested the product. Published reviews are based on research, not fabricated hands-on claims.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rt-card rt-card--progress">
          <h3>Research in progress</h3>
          <p>We are actively gathering data on this product. No score has been assigned yet. Placeholder content is clearly marked and not presented as a verdict.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>How affiliate links work</h2>
      <p>PickNotch uses affiliate links. When you click a link and buy a product, we may earn a small commission from the retailer — at no extra cost to you.</p>
      <p>Here is what that means for our reviews:</p>
      <ul class="method-list">
        <li>Affiliate links are present regardless of our score. A product with a 6/10 score still has an affiliate link if we cover it.</li>
        <li>Affiliate relationships do not guarantee positive coverage. We will not inflate a score because a brand pays better commissions.</li>
        <li>If a product we cover stops being available through affiliate channels, our review stays up. We do not remove coverage based on monetisation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We earn less money from honest reviews than from fake glowing ones. We do it anyway.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="method-section">
      <h2>How often reviews are updated</h2>
      <p>Product prices, availability, and firmware change. We update reviews when:</p>
      <ul class="method-list">
        <li>The product receives a significant firmware or hardware update</li>
        <li>The price changes substantially</li>
        <li>New owner data significantly changes the support or reliability picture</li>
        <li>A better alternative appears that changes our recommendation</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Every review shows a "last updated" date. If a review is older than 12 months in a fast-moving category, treat it with more caution.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>

<style>
.page-hero { background: var(--ink); padding: 52px 0 48px; }
.page-hero .eyebrow { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--cyan); margin: 0 0 8px; }
.page-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 36px); font-weight: 800; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 10px; }
.page-sub { font-size: 16px; color: #7A90B0; margin: 0; line-height: 1.65; }
.method-body { padding: 52px 24px 80px; }
.method-section { margin-bottom: 52px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 52px; }
.method-section:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.method-section h2 { font-size: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 26px); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--ink); }
.method-section p { font-size: 16px; color: #334155; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 16px; }
.method-section em { font-style: italic; }
.method-list { padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 16px; color: #334155; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; }
.method-list li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.criteria-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; margin-top: 20px; }
.criteria-card { display: flex; gap: 14px; background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 18px; }
.criteria-n { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cyan); flex-shrink: 0; min-width: 24px; margin-top: 2px; }
.criteria-title { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 5px; color: var(--ink); }
.criteria-body { font-size: 13px; color: var(--slate); margin: 0; line-height: 1.55; }
.score-guide { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; margin: 16px 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
.sg-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 100px 100px 1fr; gap: 16px; align-items: center; padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 14px; }
.sg-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.sg-range { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink); }
.sg-label { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; color: var(--slate); }
.sg-desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--slate); }
.method-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--slate); background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--cyan); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 12px 14px; margin: 0 !important; }
.review-type-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; margin-top: 16px; }
.rt-card { background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; }
.rt-card--published { border-top: 3px solid #0D9488; }
.rt-card--progress  { border-top: 3px solid var(--muted); }
.rt-card h3 { font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--ink); }
.rt-card p { font-size: 14px; color: #334155; margin: 0 0 8px; line-height: 1.6; }
.rt-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.rt-note strong { color: var(--ink); }
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .criteria-grid, .review-type-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .sg-row { grid-template-columns: 90px 80px 1fr; gap: 10px; }
}
</style>
